# Files that belong in the repo but not in a release archive.
#
# `git archive` builds the download from tracked files, so the zip is clean by construction — no
# Binaries/, Intermediate/ or Saved/ can leak into it, because they were never committed. These are the
# few things that *are* committed but mean nothing to someone dropping the plugin into their project.
.gitignore      export-ignore
.gitattributes  export-ignore
.github/        export-ignore

# Maintainer tooling, for the same reason .github/ is excluded: it verifies the *claim* this repo makes
# about engine support, which is a release-engineering concern. Someone dropping the plugin into their
# project has no use for it, and a stray .ps1 in a plugin folder invites the question of whether they
# are meant to run it.
Tooling/        export-ignore
